{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 12, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "texalu nr: reads through the texture unit under cal (cost 76.75 as written):\n  cost 19  fetch_repeat_offset([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x, 1) + fetch_repeat([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x)\n      [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][(7y + (x + 1) % 7) % 49] is fetch_repeat_offset([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x, 1)\n      [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][(7((y + 1) % 7) + x) % 49] is fetch_repeat([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x)\n      holds where the read is defined: there (7y + (x + 1) % 7) % 49 = x + 1 mod 7\n      the read takes x with a ConstOffset of 1 (Vulkan's minTexelOffset is at most -8 and its maxTexelOffset at least 7): the unit adds it before the address mode, the add goes\n      holds where the read is defined: there (7((y + 1) % 7) + x) % 49 = x mod 7\n      that identity between integers is proved: exhaustive\n      the coordinate (i + 1/2)/n is made in f32: within (|i| + 1/2) 2^-23 <= 7.75e-07 of a texel's centre for i in [0, 6] (its range), and the unit snaps by less than 2^-8: 7.75e-07 + 0.00391 < 1/2, the texel is i's\n      that identity between integers is proved: exhaustive\n      the coordinate (i + 1/2)/n is made in f32: within (|i| + 1/2) 2^-23 <= 7.75e-07 of a texel's centre for i in [0, 6] (its range), and the unit snaps by less than 2^-8: 7.75e-07 + 0.00391 < 1/2, the texel is i's\n      the pipeline needs (a proposal: nothing is applied):\n        a texture R8_UINT, 7 x 1, one level, its texels the table's entries\n        a sampler: NEAREST filters, REPEAT, normalised coordinates, lod 0\n        one combined image sampler more in the layout; the shader reads textureLodOffset(s, (float(x) + 0.5) * (1.0 / 7.0), 0.0, 1).r\n        a texture R8_UINT, 7 x 1, one level, its texels the table's entries\n        a sampler: NEAREST filters, REPEAT, normalised coordinates, lod 0\n        one combined image sampler more in the layout; the shader reads textureLod(s, (float(i) + 0.5) * (1.0 / 7.0), 0.0).r\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 12, "ok": true, "cmd": "texalu", "ucas": "texalu nr under cal", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "texalu", "model": "cal", "cost_before": 76.75, "status": "proved", "cost": 19, "expr": "fetch_repeat_offset([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x, 1) + fetch_repeat([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x)", "exact": true, "reads": ["[10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][(7y + (x + 1) % 7) % 49] is fetch_repeat_offset([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x, 1)", "[10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][(7((y + 1) % 7) + x) % 49] is fetch_repeat([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x)"], "holds_where": "holds where the read is defined: there (7y + (x + 1) % 7) % 49 = x + 1 mod 7\nthe read takes x with a ConstOffset of 1 (Vulkan's minTexelOffset is at most -8 and its maxTexelOffset at least 7): the unit adds it before the address mode, the add goes\nholds where the read is defined: there (7((y + 1) % 7) + x) % 49 = x mod 7", "derivation": ["that identity between integers is proved: exhaustive", "the coordinate (i + 1/2)/n is made in f32: within (|i| + 1/2) 2^-23 <= 7.75e-07 of a texel's centre for i in [0, 6] (its range), and the unit snaps by less than 2^-8: 7.75e-07 + 0.00391 < 1/2, the texel is i's", "that identity between integers is proved: exhaustive", "the coordinate (i + 1/2)/n is made in f32: within (|i| + 1/2) 2^-23 <= 7.75e-07 of a texel's centre for i in [0, 6] (its range), and the unit snaps by less than 2^-8: 7.75e-07 + 0.00391 < 1/2, the texel is i's"], "pipeline": ["a texture R8_UINT, 7 x 1, one level, its texels the table's entries", "a sampler: NEAREST filters, REPEAT, normalised coordinates, lod 0", "one combined image sampler more in the layout; the shader reads textureLodOffset(s, (float(x) + 0.5) * (1.0 / 7.0), 0.0, 1).r", "a texture R8_UINT, 7 x 1, one level, its texels the table's entries", "a sampler: NEAREST filters, REPEAT, normalised coordinates, lod 0", "one combined image sampler more in the layout; the shader reads textureL