{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 15, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "texalu nb: reads through the texture unit under cal (cost 32.625 as written):\n  cost 29.75 (x == 0 ? 99 : [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][x - 1]) + [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][x] + fetch_border_offset([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x, 99, 1)\n      x == 6 ? 99 : [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][x + 1] is fetch_border_offset([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x, 99, 1)\n      holds where the read is defined: there the condition is 0 <= x + 1 < 7, the other arm the border's value\n      the read takes x with a ConstOffset of 1 (Vulkan's minTexelOffset is at most -8 and its maxTexelOffset at least 7): the unit adds it before the address mode, the add goes\n      that identity between integers is proved: exhaustive\n      the coordinate (i + 1/2)/n is made in f32: within (|i| + 1/2) 2^-23 <= 7.75e-07 of a texel's centre for i in [0, 6] (its range), and the unit snaps by less than 2^-8: 7.75e-07 + 0.00391 < 1/2, the texel is i's\n      the pipeline needs (a proposal: nothing is applied):\n        a texture R8_UINT, 7 x 1, one level, its texels the table's entries\n        a sampler: NEAREST filters, CLAMP_TO_BORDER with the border's value as a custom border colour (VK_EXT_custom_border_color), normalised coordinates, lod 0\n        one combined image sampler more in the layout; the shader reads textureLodOffset(s, (float(x) + 0.5) * (1.0 / 7.0), 0.0, 1).r\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 15, "ok": true, "cmd": "texalu", "ucas": "texalu nb under cal", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "texalu", "model": "cal", "cost_before": 32.625, "status": "proved", "cost": 29.75, "expr": "(x == 0 ? 99 : [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][x - 1]) + [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][x] + fetch_border_offset([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x, 99, 1)", "exact": true, "reads": ["x == 6 ? 99 : [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70][x + 1] is fetch_border_offset([10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70], x, 99, 1)"], "holds_where": "holds where the read i